# ESLint ignore list for the Blitzy skin.
#
# Keep this list minimal. Every entry below is a silent exemption from the
# zero-warning build gate, so nothing this package authors may appear here:
# when a source file fails lint, fix the file, never add it to this list.
#
# `eslint .` does not only walk `.js`. eslint-config-wikimedia declares
# overrides for `**/*.json`, `**/*.jsonc`, `**/*.yaml`, `**/*.yml` and
# `**/*.ts`, and ESLint adds those extensions to its directory traversal, so
# manifests, message catalogues, Compose files and TypeScript specs are all
# lint targets here. It also un-ignores dotfiles that carry an extension
# (`.eslintrc.json`, `.stylelintrc.json`, `.svgo.config.js` are linted) while
# already excluding the contents of dot-directories, which is why `.cache/`
# and `.playwright/` need no entry of their own.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and why:
#   resources/skins.blitzy.js/  the client script; progressive enhancement is a
#                               hard requirement, so this code is linted.
#   tests/qunit/                the client unit suites that earn the coverage
#                               floor; linted like production code.
#   tools/, karma.conf.js, .svgo.config.js
#                               package tooling; linted.
#   playwright.config.ts, tests/playwright/**/*.ts
#                               linted as-is. The pinned eslint-config-wikimedia
#                               already depends on @typescript-eslint/parser and
#                               applies its TypeScript profile to `**/*.ts`, so
#                               no extra parser and no new build tooling are
#                               needed. An unlinted spec is exactly where a
#                               stray `test.skip` or a swallowed assertion
#                               hides, and fidelity assertions must fail rather
#                               than skip.
#   screenshots/, design/       committed deliverables. `screenshots/audits/`
#                               holds generated JSON that is linted like any
#                               other JSON, so the generators must write it
#                               tab-indented with a trailing newline rather
#                               than have this list excuse them.

# Dependency trees: third-party code this package installs but does not author.
/node_modules/
/vendor/

# Generated reports and transient test-runner output. Never committed, never
# authored here, and written by their tools with formatting ESLint rejects.
/coverage/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# Message catalogues. Validated by banana-checker, which checks key
# completeness and qqq documentation: obligations ESLint cannot express.
/i18n/
